Task t0-even-odd: count even and odd.

```
Trepiho even := 0;
Trepiho odd := 0;
Trepiho line := Thoke();
Rokomi (line ~= Krupelro) {
    Trepiho n := Eshiyer(line);
    Mushu n % 2 = 0 Yeshil Hupo
        even := even + 1;
    Tho Thotri Hupo
        odd := odd + 1;
    Tho
    line := Thoke();
}
Rashar "even " + even;
Rashar "odd " + odd;
```

Note: negative numbers — `-7 % 2` is `-1`, not 0, so `-7` would be counted odd. That's correct since -7 is odd. For even negatives like `-4 % 2 = 0`, fine. Good.

Task t0-factorial: n 0..20. 20! = 2432902008176640000 which fits in 64-bit (max ~9.2e18). So plain multiplication works.

```
Trepiho n := Eshiyer(Thoke());
Trepiho result := 1;
Pil (Trepiho i := 2; i <= n; i := i + 1) {
    result := result * i;
}
Rashar result;
```

Or recursive. Iterative is fine.

